      "spam": false,
      "value": "That is probably due to your processor. Vrchat is very CPU intsensive when it comes to many avatars in one instance and your processor is really not up to that job. I suspect that things will get really laggy for you starting at around 20 people. Also VRChat uses large amounts of ram so you might want to keep programs like google chrome from running in the background. I sometimes run out of ram when having chrome and vrchat open with my 16GB of ram. So yeah you could probably install additional ram if that is your problem. You could also try overclocking your cpu to maybe squeeze some more performance out of it, if you really cannot or dont want to afford a better one.",
      "viewerReactions": null
    },
